  subtitle="Command surface defined in packages/nikcli/src/index.ts and packages/nikcli/src/cli/cmd."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="entry-point" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Entry Point</h2>
    <p>
      Running <code>nikcli</code> without a subcommand opens the default terminal UI (TUI) in the
      current directory. Pass an optional project path to open the TUI in another directory. Global
      flags <code>--print-logs</code> and <code>--log-level</code> apply to every command.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="bash">
      nikcli                    # open TUI in current directory
      nikcli /path/to/project   # open TUI in another project
      nikcli --help             # list all commands
      nikcli completion         # generate shell completion script
    </DocCode>
    <DocCallout type="info" title="Default TUI">
      <p>
        The default TUI command is <code>$0 [project]</code> and accepts session, model, agent,
        continue, prompt, and network flags. All options available to <code>nikcli run</code> are
        also accepted here.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="interactive-workflows" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Interactive Workflows</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Command</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>nikcli [project]</code></td>
          <td>Open the TUI in the current or specified project directory.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>nikcli run [message..]</code></td>
          <td>Run a one-shot prompt without entering the TUI.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>nikcli attach &lt;url&gt;</code></td>
          <td>Attach a local TUI to a shared remote session URL.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>nikcli session list</code></td>
          <td>List past and active sessions.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>nikcli quickstart</code></td>
          <td>Interactive walkthrough for first-time users. Accepts <code>--skip-checks</code> and <code>--dry-run</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>nikcli pr &lt;number&gt;</code></td>
          <td>Fetch and checkout a GitHub PR branch, then launch nikcli in the resulting worktree.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <DocCode language="bash">
      nikcli run "audit this repo and summarize risks"
      nikcli attach https://example.nikcli.store/share/abcd
      nikcli quickstart --skip-checks
      nikcli pr 42
    </DocCode>
  </section>

  <section id="autonomous-scheduled" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Autonomous &amp; Scheduled</h2>
    <p>
      <code>goal</code> drives the agent autonomously until a verifiable condition is met.
      <code>routine</code> manages saved prompts with scheduled (cron) or API triggers.
    </p>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Command</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>nikcli goal [condition..]</code></td>
          <td>
            Work autonomously until the stated condition is met. Flags: <code>--continue</code>,
            <code>--session</code>, <code>--model</code>, <code>--agent</code>,
            <code>--variant</code>, <code>--token-budget</code>, <code>--format</code>.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>nikcli routine list</code></td>
          <td>List all routines for the current project.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>nikcli routine create</code></td>
          <td>Create a routine interactively or with flags. See the <a href="/docs/routines">Routines</a> page.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>nikcli routine get &lt;id&gt;</code></td>
          <td>Show details of a specific routine.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>nikcli routine run &lt;id&gt;</code></td>
          <td>Trigger an immediate run of a routine.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>nikcli routine pause &lt;id&gt;</code></td>
          <td>Pause a routine (disables its scheduled triggers).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>nikcli routine resume &lt;id&gt;</code></td>
          <td>Resume a paused routine.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>nikcli routine delete &lt;id&gt;</code></td>
          <td>Delete a routine (alias: <code>rm</code>). Prompts for confirmation unless <code>--yes</code> is passed.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <DocCode language="bash">
      nikcli goal "all tests pass and no lint errors"
      nikcli goal --token-budget 50000 "fix the failing integration test"
      nikcli routine create --name "daily review" --prompt "summarize recent changes" --cron @daily
      nikcli routine run rtn_abc123
    </DocCode>
  </section>

